tack list
.EE
.SH TROUBLESHOOTING
\f[B]Common issues:\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
If tack fails with \(lqdoes not look like a Tack\-able site
directory\(rq, ensure your site directory contains both
\f[CR]content/\f[R] and \f[CR]templates/\f[R] subdirectories.
.IP \(bu 2
Use the \f[CR]\-d\f[R] flag to enable debug output when troubleshooting
build issues.
.IP \(bu 2
Use the \f[CR]\-s\f[R] flag to enable strict mode, which will fail if
any undefined variables are referenced in templates, helping catch
template errors.
.IP \(bu 2
Use \f[CR]tack list\f[R] to verify that tack is detecting and organizing
your pages correctly.
.IP \(bu 2
The \f[CR]serve\f[R] command automatically rebuilds when files change,
but only checks for changes every 3 seconds.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Tack returns a non\-zero exit code if tacking the website was not
successful due to being unable to read or process any of the input files
or if the \f[I]output\f[R] directory cannot be written to.
